"<p>Nitrobase can manage both the machine it runs on (<em>Localhost</em>) and any number of remote <strong>Ubuntu or Debian</strong> servers over SSH.</p>\n<h2>Adding a Remote Server</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Navigate to <strong>Servers → Add Server</strong>.</li>\n<li>Enter the server details:\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Host IP / Hostname</strong></li>\n<li><strong>SSH Port</strong> (default <code>22</code>)</li>\n<li><strong>Username</strong> (default <code>root</code>)</li>\n<li><strong>Authentication:</strong> Select an SSH key (managed under <strong>Settings → SSH keys</strong>) or password authentication.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Test the connection to verify SSH reachability and host key fingerprint.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Guided Server Bootstrap</h2>\n<p>Before touching your server, <strong>Bootstrap</strong> inspects the host and shows an explicit preview of every change it will make:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>OS &#x26; packages:</strong> Verifies Ubuntu or Debian (<code>/etc/os-release</code>) and installs missing base tools (<code>ca-certificates</code>, <code>curl</code>, <code>wget</code>, <code>git</code>, <code>jq</code>, <code>openssl</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>Docker Engine:</strong> Installs <code>docker-ce</code>, <code>docker-ce-cli</code>, <code>containerd.io</code>, <code>docker-buildx-plugin</code>, and <code>docker-compose-plugin</code> from Docker's official apt repository if missing, and enables the <code>docker</code> service.</li>\n<li><strong>Directory layout:</strong> Creates <code>/etc/nitrobase</code> (<code>apps/</code>, <code>traefik/dynamic/</code>, <code>traefik/acme/</code>, <code>logs/</code>, etc.).</li>\n<li><strong>Shared proxy network:</strong> Creates the <code>nitrobase-network</code> Docker bridge network.</li>\n<li><strong>Traefik v3:</strong> Starts the <code>nitrobase-traefik</code> container (<code>traefik:v3.6.25</code> by default) with dynamic file routing and Let's Encrypt ACME support.</li>\n<li><strong>Firewall &#x26; port checks:</strong> Checks whether ports <code>80</code> and <code>443</code> are reachable/available (or skips public port checks when configured for Cloudflare Tunnel only).</li>\n<li><strong>Ownership marker:</strong> Labels the Traefik container with <code>nitrobase.instance=&#x3C;instanceId></code> so two Nitrobase panels never accidentally manage and fight over the same server.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Server Resource Limits</h2>\n<p>Under <strong>Server → Settings → Resource limits</strong>, administrators can require memory/CPU limits on every service deployed to that server. During app pre-flight, Nitrobase warns when the sum of configured memory or CPU limits across apps would exceed <code>RESOURCE_OVERCOMMIT_PERCENT</code> (default <code>100%</code>) of the server's hardware.</p>"